From: q56-scratch <q56@scratch>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:31:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] src: text1a_c2 / text1a_b / text1a_b_pre_rodata / sound /
 text1b declarations reconciled by evidence (owner rulings Q65/Q67, step 8)

text1a_c2, text1a_b, text1a_b_pre_rodata, sound and text1b are one original file (owner ruling Q67;
text1a_b_pre_rodata joins under (A7), owner ruling Q72). Each symbol they declare differently gets one type
before the merge. The per-symbol evidence is in the step script's docstring (tmp/q56/adopt/s08_apply.py).
The parts stay separate files in this commit.

Owner-decided types (per-file-gp-model.md (A5), owner ruling Q70):
- D_80102C00 keeps s32. Its only use is taking its address.
- func_8004153C keeps the unprototyped `extern s32 *func_8004153C();`. The tidy-up is deferred.
- D_800153F0 is a 22-halfword struct, copied in one assignment.
- func_80044100 is declared unprototyped, `extern void func_80044100();` (owner ruling Q88, rules: a17a2c144,
  added to A5): text1a_b calls it with one argument ($a1 unset in the target), sound with two.
- sound's func_800475A4 / camera_CalcAngles hand SVECTOR / VECTOR / MATRIX locals to the libgte calls
  (layer-2 round 2): no casts on s16[3] / s32[3..8] buffers; byte-identical.

Byte-identity proof for D_800153F0 (A5 requires it banked here):
- func_8004A09C reads the 44 bytes as u16.
- func_80049F4C's original copy carries a run-time alignment test: or/andi 3/beqz, then an lwl/lwr +
  swl/swr loop or an lw/sw loop. That is GCC's block move when the compile-time alignment is below 4.
- In one file whose definition precedes the copy, varasm's DATA_ALIGNMENT (config/mips/mips.h) raises
  DECL_ALIGN of any aggregate definition to 32 (varasm.c "Reset the alignment ... get_pointer_alignment").
  So a copy through the object's address would be compile-time aligned and carry no test.
- A struct ASSIGNMENT passes the type's alignment, 2, to emit_block_move. That reproduces the test.

Measured:
- Before the merge, every src/*.c object is byte-identical (objcompare).
- In the merged file (step 09), the full build is the oracle.
- The definition text1a_b_pre_rodata.c emits the same 44 bytes. Each little-endian word becomes two
  halfwords, low first; alignment stays 4 (DATA_ALIGNMENT).

Body changes, each needing its own layer-2:
- game_StageCleanup and game_GetPlayerData forward their argument registers.
- func_800486FC returns s32.
- func_80049F4C uses the struct assignment.
- Cast-only call-site edits in sound, text1a_c2 and text1b.
